                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] RANDOM STEAM GAME [/h1]\n\nI look all over Steam for random / unknown Steam games to play. This was one of the chosen titles this week! If you'd rather watch than read, you can do so here:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lk4lDj5Zd3Q\n\n[b] [Thoughts and First Impressions] [/b]\n\nOKAY. I have a lot of thoughts on this one. First off, it's not worth the 10$ asking price for this game. That should be very obvious by my negative review. One of the big downsides of this game is just how SIMPLE the game is. It's too simple for it's own good. Enemies have sloppy animations and little movement besides moving left and right on the screen. You have a weak attack and a heavy attack and that's basically it. Yes you can do a fancier hit in the air if you can knock an enemy up, but that becomes useless once you realize that most enemies can't be knocked up into the air in the first place. Oh right, your \"ultimate\" attack - It's a dash forward with a blue line that just kind of does some extra damage. It's not good.\n\nEach level consists of a small stage that takes 10 seconds to cross and you have to eliminate 5 - 8 enemies and you get to move on. Yes that's it. If you die on hard mode then you have to go back to the very first level. If you play on light mode you can restart from that level. You also keep health between stages and get very little healing throughout. The boss fights are generally forgettable and just consist of you jumping and avoiding their attacks and then getting a few hits in. No most attacks aren't hard to dodge. Just run in and tap attack.\n\nThis game is just missing anything resembling fun and challenge. It's bland. It has no real flavor to it. The enemies could have been generic squares and you pretty much wouldn't change anything about the aesthetic. \n\ntl;dr - The game is boring.\n\nJoin the Curator group for more reviews and \"unboxing\" of unknown games! https://store.steampowered.com/curator/34634494/",
